<p>Two sailboats carrying humanitarian aid from southern Mexico arrived in Havana on Saturday after losing contact at sea. The Mexican Navy later found them off Cuba&#x27;s coast and escorted them into port. Organizers said everyone aboard was safe, ending several days of uncertainty around the trip. The boats were part of an aid convoy bound for Cuba as the island struggles with shortages of food, medicine and fuel. Their arrival brought a reassuring end to a mission meant to deliver relief supplies to the island.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/d3_FJGXQ9Dej-3rlHBeBh7XWCbzeqD0K1fYbCr-ePjPhTTy4fwEFHGEQseW96owVq1EUjQTCUC5MXYjh9xpJadmElAezj64b0fsXFDBkSm6s6YyZXKMjMgNPGn5kh-lNF7nWpmVm3HBqqiQi27peM3FRw0pichHiV4Fm38OopKQ06j9fraPYYZJ35QrA0AV7pWwbp_NDHlaWuzhyU1mnUude7pO0sGw7H0Y_wSrVgB07ZRKNXZiNF62XPlUsEUxhq2AehgFiXzr9dKVPbQ' alt='Activists wave Cuban and Palestinian flags from the vessel Maguro, arriving from Mexico with humanitarian aid as part of the &quot;Nuestra America,&quot; or Our America Convoy, in Havana Bay, Cuba, Tuesday, March 24, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Nine aboard: The two vessels carried nine people in total when they left southern Mexico before communications were lost.</li><li>Weather delay: Coordinator Adnaan Stumo said rough weather forced the boats onto a longer route and delayed their arrival, though he said the sailors were never in serious danger.</li><li>Convoy name: The aid mission was part of the &quot;Nuestra America,&quot; or &quot;Our America Convoy,&quot; according to reporting from Havana on the arrival.</li><li>Afternoon landing: CBS said the two sailboats reached Havana on Saturday afternoon.</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/missing-cuba-bound-boats-carrying-aid-arrive-safely-in-havana/a-76580010'>Missing Cuba-bound boats carrying aid arrive safely in Havana</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/missing-sailboats-carrying-aid-arrive-in-cuba-after-be